.TH CCACHE_INIT 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccache_init \- initialise a previously declared LRU cache variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

ccache_init(name, capacity, getter, setter, evict_cb);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls clrucache_create_full() and assigns the result to name, with the
key type and the value type taken from the companion variables that
ccache_declare() created. It calls _ccol_fatal_err() when the creation
fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name       Cache variable. Declare it with ccache_declare or
           ccache_declare_scoped first
capacity   The total number of live entries; see
           clrucache_create_full(3). It must be greater than 0
getter     Remote getter callback, or NULL
setter     Remote setter callback, or NULL
evict_cb   Eviction callback, or NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro calls _ccol_fatal_err() when an allocation fails, so call
clrucache_create_full() directly when you must handle an error
yourself.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccache_declare(cache, int, double);
ccache_init(cache, 64, NULL, NULL, NULL);
ccache_destroy(cache);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccache_declare (3),
.BR ccache_construct (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
